Observational astronomy (@observational-astronomy: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_2KGHM1GMWSY7YXY9RH3JG4KMDW
Observational astronomy acquires and interprets evidence about celestial objects through light and other messengers. The material connects telescopes, detectors, spectroscopy, timing, surveys, calibration, and data analysis with observatory operations and the limits imposed by instruments and observing conditions.

**Common preparation developed:** the [causal signals and received-frequency lesson](../../core/Preserve-causal-order-and-distinguish-clock-rates-from-received-frequencies.lingua) distinguishes coordinate clock rates, emission/reception delay and the longitudinal Doppler comparison. Orbital and weak-clock preparation is developed; the subsequent astronomical foundation now connects distance, spectra, brightness, detectors and bounded observational inference.

**Common preparation developed:** the [astronomical evidence review](../../core/Review-astronomical-evidence-before-opening-the-major-branches.lingua) connects directions, parallax and its inference limits, photon counts, calibration, brightness and spectra, orbital projection and published-calculation criticism. Full instrumentation, survey analysis, observatory operations and advanced practical formation remain pending.

**Parent:** [Universe and space](../Universe-and-space.lingua#r_38KB376VFZ30BXTGB9K0HG55ZP).
} r_2KGHM1GMWSY7YXY9RH3JG4KMDW
